# factory-reach-image.env — the sandbox image ./verify-factory-reach.sh renders
# into the Job it submits (livespec-dev-tooling-jvnqwv, livespec plan
# factory-worker-nodes-gitops, epic livespec-sqvj7p; freeze ruling R70,
# 2026-10-16).
#
# FORMAT: one `FACTORY_REACH_SANDBOX_IMAGE=<ref>` line; `#` comments and blank
# lines ignored. The renderer refuses a file naming two values rather than
# picking one — which toolchain the probe runs is a real question, and guessing
# it wrong proves a pull nobody performs. Override with `--image REF`, or point
# at another file with `--image-file FILE`.
#
# WHY THE PIN SHIPS HERE AND NOT IN ../../../../.github/workflows/ci.yml, WHICH
# IS WHERE THIS CHECK USED TO READ IT. R70 made the check a converge artifact:
# ../../../../ansible/roles/factory_reach_check installs the four files of this
# set into the node's installed tree, and that tree carries NO repository
# checkout — so the workflow the first version read is simply not on the node.
# ../gates/render-gate-job.sh still reads the workflow, and correctly: it runs
# from a checkout on the control node, where the file exists. The two resolve
# the same pin from different places because they run in different places.
#
# IT IS THE FLEET SANDBOX IMAGE PIN, AND NOTHING KEEPS A SECOND COPY HONEST BY
# ITSELF. The release fan-out rewrites the `container:` `image:` pin in
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml` on every release; this file is a second copy of
# that same reference, so `livespec_dev_tooling/fabro_image_pin_lockstep.py`
# fails when the two differ. A release bump that moves the workflow pin and
# leaves this one behind therefore reddens rather than quietly rendering a Job
# that pulls a superseded image. Bump BOTH, in the same change.
FACTORY_REACH_SANDBOX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/thewoolleyman/livespec-fabro-sandbox:python-v1.146.3
